[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # ERRORS.md — Phase C error-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` and `c_src/include/lib.h`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Grep audit of every rejection mechanism the C source could use:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```sh
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -nE 'RETURN_ERROR|return -1|return NULL|assert|errno|ERROR|MIN|MAX|default:|return 0' \
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     src/lib.c include/lib.h
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Result: the library contains **no** `assert`, **no** `errno`, **no** error enum,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **no** `return -1` / `return NULL`, **no** explicit range/null check, and **no**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `MIN`/`MAX` constants. The *only* rejection construct in the whole library is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `default:` label of the three `switch` statements in `collided`, each of which
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m does `return 0`. Everything else is unchecked arithmetic whose "rejection" is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m floating-point `comiss`/`seta` comparison evaluating false (the NaN case).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows 1–3 are the three literal `default: return 0` branches (lib.c:81-82,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lib.c:91-92, lib.c:95-96). Rows 4–13 are the generic FFI boundaries required by
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Phase C (out-of-range enum values, null pointers, sentinel/NaN rejection,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m one-step-past-valid-range enum values).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `collided` (lib.c:95-96, outer `default:`) | `typeA` is not `C2_TYPE_CIRCLE(0)` nor `C2_TYPE_AABB(1)` — e.g. `2`, `3`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MAX`, `0x7fffffff`. `typeB` and both pointers irrelevant (pointers are **not** dereferenced). | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `collided` (lib.c:81-82, inner `default:` under `C2_TYPE_CIRCLE`) | `typeA == 0` and `typeB` out of range (`2`, `-1`, `INT_MAX`, …). `A` is not dereferenced. | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `collided` (lib.c:91-92, inner `default:` under `C2_TYPE_AABB`) | `typeA == 1` and `typeB` out of range (`2`, `-1`, `INT_MAX`, …). `A` is not dereferenced. | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `collided` | `typeA` one step past the valid range: `typeA == 2` (`C2_TYPE_AABB + 1`) with every `typeB` in `{0,1,2}` | returns `0` (row 1 path) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `collided` | `typeB` one step past the valid range: `typeB == 2` with `typeA` in `{0,1}` | returns `0` (rows 2/3 path) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `collided` | Null pointers with an out-of-range `typeA` (`A == NULL`, `B == NULL`, `typeA == 2`) — the switch rejects before any dereference, so this is defined behaviour | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 7 | `collided` | Null `B` with `typeA == 0`, `typeB == 2` — inner `default:` reached before `B` is dereferenced | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `collided` | Null `B` with `typeA == 1`, `typeB == 2` | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `collided` | Non-null but *unaligned* / oversized-read shapes: `A` points at a `c2AABB` (16 B) while `typeA == C2_TYPE_CIRCLE` (12 B read) and vice versa — C reinterprets the bytes with no check; Rust must reinterpret identically | same `int` as C for the reinterpreted bytes |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `c2CircletoCircle` | `A.r` or `B.r` is `NaN` ⇒ `r2` is `NaN` ⇒ `comiss` unordered ⇒ `seta` false | returns `0` (no error code, sentinel rejection) |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 11 | `c2CircletoCircle` / `c2CircletoAABB` | any input coordinate is `NaN` ⇒ `d2` is `NaN` ⇒ unordered compare | returns `0` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 12 | `c2CircletoCircle` / `c2CircletoAABB` | negative radius (`A.r < 0`): **not** rejected by C — `r2 = r*r` is positive, so a negative radius behaves like its absolute value | returns the same as `|r|`; must not be "fixed" |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 13 | `c2AABBtoAABB` | inverted / degenerate box (`min > max`, `min == max`, `NaN` corner): no validation; result is `!(d0|d1|d2|d3)` over the four unordered-false comparisons | `1` whenever all four `<` are false (so an all-`NaN` box "collides") |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Notes on untestable-by-design cases
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Dereferencing a genuinely null pointer with a *valid* type tag
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`collided(NULL, C2_TYPE_CIRCLE, …)`) is undefined behaviour in the C — it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m segfaults. It is therefore **not** part of the error surface (the C does not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "reject" it) and is deliberately not exercised as a differential test; doing so
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m would crash both libraries rather than compare them. Rows 6–8 cover the null
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pointer cases that the C actually *defines* (rejected by the switch before any
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m dereference).
