[49m[38;5;10m+      1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c` + `c_src/include/lib.h`, plus the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m compiled C `.so` disassembly (the C is built with **no** optimisation flags —
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets none — so every helper is a real `call` through the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m PLT and every FP operation is a discrete `mulss`/`addss`/`subss`/`comiss`; the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m operand order in that asm is part of the observable behaviour for NaN payloads).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 1 — entry point.** There are 10 exported functions, only *one* of which
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`collided`) is declared in the public header. The other nine are the low-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m API and are exercised directly, not only through the `collided` wrapper:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2V`, `c2Maxv`, `c2Minv`, `c2Clampv`, `c2Sub`, `c2Dot`, `c2CircletoCircle`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2CircletoAABB`, `c2AABBtoAABB`, `collided`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 2 — runtime option/mode.** The only runtime option the public API can set
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is the `C2_TYPE` tag pair `(typeA, typeB)` passed to `collided`. Valid states:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `(CIRCLE,CIRCLE)`, `(CIRCLE,AABB)`, `(AABB,CIRCLE)`, `(AABB,AABB)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Note `(AABB,CIRCLE)` (lib.c:89-90) dispatches to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2CircletoAABB(*(c2Circle*)B, *(c2AABB*)A)` — the *swapped* operand order, a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m distinct code path from `(CIRCLE,AABB)`. There are no `#ifdef`s and no other
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m flags (`grep -c '#if' → 0`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 3 — control-flow branches inside the math.** 13 branch/ternary sites:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the 2 ternaries in `c2Maxv`, the 2 in `c2Minv`, the 4 `<` comparisons in
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c2AABBtoAABB`, the 2 `d2 < r2` compares, and the 3 `switch`es. Each ternary
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m takes the *else* arm for NaN (`comiss`+`jbe`), so NaN-vs-finite ordering is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m distinct configuration from finite-vs-finite.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 4 — input value shape (float bit classes).** The code does no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m classification, but the hardware does: `+/-` normal, `+0.0`, `-0.0`, subnormal,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `+inf`, `-inf`, QNaN (payload-carrying), SNaN (quieted by the ALU), and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m magnitudes large enough that `r*r` / `d2` overflow to `inf`, or small enough that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `x*x` underflows to `0`/subnormal.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Axis 5 — geometric shape.** overlapping, exactly touching (`d2 == r2`, the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m strict-`<` boundary), disjoint, one shape fully inside the other, circle centre
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inside the AABB (clamp is a no-op ⇒ `d2 == 0`), zero radius, negative radius,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m inverted AABB (`min > max`), degenerate AABB (`min == max`), and box/circle
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m struct sizes mismatching the tag (12-byte `c2Circle` vs 16-byte `c2AABB`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reinterpretation).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each row is checked off only after **many randomized inputs** (fixed seed,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m property-style) pass byte-for-byte against the C `.so`. Test names refer to
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/tests/differential.rs`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 1 | `c2V` | random finite `f32` bit patterns; asserts returned struct bits identical (pure struct-return ABI check) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 2 | `c2V` | special values: `±0.0`, `±inf`, subnormals, QNaN & SNaN payloads (must pass through unquieted — no arithmetic) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 3 | `c2Maxv` | both components finite normals, all orderings (`a>b`, `a<b`, `a==b`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 4 | `c2Maxv` | `±0.0` mixes (`+0.0 > -0.0` is false ⇒ returns `b`) and subnormals | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 5 | `c2Maxv` | NaN in `a` only / `b` only / both, with distinct payloads ⇒ else-arm (`b`) taken, payload preserved | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 6 | `c2Maxv` | `±inf` operands, mixed with finites and NaN | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 7 | `c2Minv` | both components finite normals, all orderings | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 8 | `c2Minv` | `±0.0` mixes and subnormals | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 9 | `c2Minv` | NaN in `a` / `b` / both with distinct payloads ⇒ else-arm (`b`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 10 | `c2Minv` | `±inf` operands mixed with finites and NaN | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 11 | `c2Clampv` | `lo <= hi`, point below / inside / above the range (composes `c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a,hi))`) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 12 | `c2Clampv` | **inverted range** `lo > hi` (unchecked by C; result is `lo`-dominated) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 13 | `c2Clampv` | NaN in `a`, in `lo`, in `hi`, and combinations — exercises the composed ternary chain, where NaN placement changes which operand survives | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 14 | `c2Clampv` | `±inf` bounds, `lo == hi` (degenerate), `±0.0` bounds | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 15 | `c2Sub` | random finite normals (`subss` per component) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 16 | `c2Sub` | overflow to `±inf` (`FLT_MAX - -FLT_MAX`), underflow to subnormal/`±0.0`, `x - x == +0.0`, `-0.0 - +0.0 == -0.0` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 17 | `c2Sub` | `inf - inf` (same sign) ⇒ QNaN indefinite `0xFFC00000`; `inf - (-inf)` ⇒ `inf` | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 18 | `c2Sub` | NaN operands with distinct payloads in `a` and/or `b` ⇒ SSE dst-preference (`a` wins), SNaN quieted | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 19 | `c2Dot` | random finite normals (checks the pinned `mulss a.x,b.x` / `mulss b.y,a.y` / `addss q,p` operand order) | [x] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | 20 | `c2Dot` | products that overflow to `±inf`, and `+inf + -inf` in the sum ⇒ QNaN indefinite | [x] |
